As for Dlvl versus Exp, it seems about right.
As for equipment, I'm not sure how much spoilage you want on the
responses, but since the guide you linked mentions these points, I
will too.
Looking at your equipment, I can tell you try armour without checking
their BUC (that is, if they are blessed, uncursed or cursed). That is
dangerous since you can get stuck with a cursed negatively enchanted
piece of armour. By dropping items (not just armour) on an altar (by
level 8 you probably have found some altar by now) you get to know
their BUC and can safely try non-cursed armour. Provided you check for
BUC, you should try more armour since some of it is generated with a
positive enchantment to lower even further your AC.
Your AC is ok for your current level, but mostly because of the
crystal plate mail. While it gives you many AC points it is very
heavy, and carrying too much stuff to the point of getting 'burdened'
is dangerous since it slows you down.
Also, that post is not long.

